{"alignments": [{"id": "ISA.15.2.a001", "note": "The finite verb takes the supplied subject, auxiliary, and phrasal predicate, headed on “gone.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.001"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a002", "note": "The article in הַבַּיִת receives no separate English determiner in the ASV proper-name rendering “Bayith.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.002"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.002", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a003", "note": "Took “to Bayith” as the directional rendering of the bare place nominal; the alternative note permits the common-noun readings “the house” or “the temple.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.003"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a004", "note": "The waw is rendered “and.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.004"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a005", "note": "The supplied directional “to” belongs to the place name.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.005"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a006", "note": "The article is rendered “the.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.006"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a007", "note": "The directional “to” is supplied for the nominal, and “high” carries the lexeme of בָּמוֹת rather than the generic noun “places.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.007"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a008", "note": "The preposition supplies the infinitival “to.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.008"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.008", "status"