"t023"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a018", "note": "The quantifier is rendered “all.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.018"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a019", "note": "The construct noun retains “heads,” while its suffix supplies the possessive.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.019"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a020", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the possessive “their.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.020"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a021", "note": "The construction-supplied copula joins the nominal predicate “baldness.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.021"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027", "t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a022", "note": "The quantifier is rendered “every.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.022"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a023", "note": "Direct nominal correspondence.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.023"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t030"], "target_head": "t030"}, {"id": "ISA.15.2.a024", "note": "The passive predicate is headed on the lexical verb “cut”; “off” is its phrasal particle.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.2.024"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.2.024", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031", "t032", "t033"], "target_head": "t032"}], "ref": "ISA.15.2", "review_notes": ["The ASV marginal alternatives allow “Bayith and Dibon are gone up to the high places” and the common-noun readings “house” or “temple”; the alignment follows the printed main text’s place-name analysis.", "The two occurrences translated “over” have the marginal alternative “upon,” without changing their morphemic ownership."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew