{"alignments": [{"id": "ISA.15.5.a001", "note": "Direct nominal correspondence.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a002", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the possessive “My.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a003", "note": "The preposition is rendered “for.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a004", "note": "Direct proper-name correspondence.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a005", "note": "The verb is rendered by the phrasal predicate “crieth out.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a006", "note": "The printed main text renders the nominal as “nobles”; the margin offers the alternative reading “fugitives.” Because the noun already has its nominal rendering, the separate predicate “flee” is not part of this unit.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a007", "note": "The ASV supplies the lexical predicate “flee” for a clause containing no corresponding Hebrew verb; its addition markup corroborates this analysis.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a008", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the possessive “her.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a009", "note": "The endpoint preposition is rendered “unto.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a010", "note": "Direct proper-name correspondence.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a011", "note": "The supplied directional “to” belongs to the first element of the place name.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a012", "note": "The ASV prints the transliteration of Shelishiyah as “shelishi yah.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a013", "note": "The discourse conjunction is rendered “for.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a014", "note": "The supplied adverbial “by” belongs to the construct noun “ascent.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.013"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a015", "note": "The rectum’s article supplies the fronted “the” for the construct phrase.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.014"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a016", "note": "As nomen rectum, Luhith takes the construct relation “of” with its name.", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.015"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "ISA.15.5.a017", "note": "The preposition is rendered “with.”", "source": ["WLC.ISA.15.5.016"], "source_head": "WLC.ISA.15.5.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t0